<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">4</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">ABB SAFETY SERIES FOOD & BEVERAGE</div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="body-text">
            <div style="two-column;">
                <div class="column">
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <span class="highlight">Production of farming inputs</span>
                        <p style="margin: 5px 0 15px 0;">e.g., seeds, fertilizers, animal feed, nutrients and equipment.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <span class="highlight">Production of raw commodities</span>
                        <p style="margin: 5px 0 15px 0;">e.g., grains, fruits, pulses, milk, meat, poultry and fish.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <span class="highlight">Initial processing</span>
                        <p style="margin: 5px 0 15px 0;">e.g., cleaning, sorting, drying, milling, and packaging of raw materials.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <span class="highlight">Conversion of raw materials</span>
                        <p style="margin: 5px 0 15px 0;">e.g., milling, brewing, baking, and bottling.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <span class="highlight">Food & beverage processing</span>
                        <p style="margin: 5px 0 15px 0;">e.g., pasteurization, sterilization, and packaging.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <span class="highlight">Distribution of finished goods</span>
                        <p style="margin: 5px 0 15px 0;">e.g., warehousing, fulfillment and transportation.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="column">
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <span class="highlight">To balance cost and regulatory pressures with the need to automate and meet rising production targets, it's valuable to look at the operations holistically. ABB's Installation Products portfolio is needed in every F&B processing application and segment.</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text" style="margin-top: 30px;">
                        <span class="highlight">Adaptability is essential.</span> Food & Beverage is a complex and constantly changing industry. Whether digitising operations or adapting to new regulatory requirements, producers are looking for ways to boost productivity, improve safety, and meet the need of new and innovative production methods. ABB's Installation Products provide the solutions that allow for faster changeovers, reduce downtime and improve overall operations.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">5</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">CONSIDERATIONS FOR BOOSTING PRODUCTIVITY AND PRESERVING SAFETY</div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column">
                <div class="body-text">
                    <div class="icon-box">
                        <span style="color: red;">&#9888;</span>
                        <p><strong>1 Productivity</strong></p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        Demand is growing and many food and beverage factories worldwide are operating 24/7 to meet higher efficiency, productivity and sustainability goals. In this era of continuous operations, uptime and on-time delivery, F&B producers need to be able to adapt production to supply changes and demand surges.
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        Every touchpoint across food and beverage production is held to high standards of safety, from personnel and practices to preparation and packaging. Not only can downtime in F&B cost thousands of dollars per line per hour, it can result in significant food waste. Overlaying the entire operations are production schedules that factor in added or extended shifts, maintenance, and cleaning and sanitation, while assuring minimal downtime.
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="column">
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <div class="icon-box">
                            <span style="color: green;">&#127752;</span>
                            <p><strong>Food Zone no contact</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="body-text">
                            Areas that include surfaces not in direct contact with food, but adjacent or in proximity to food contact surfaces.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <div class="icon-box">
                            <span style="color: orange;">&#128270;</span>
                            <p><strong>Food Zone</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="body-text">
                            Areas that are in direct contact with food, but not surfaces intended for contact with consumable food.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <div class="icon-box">
                            <span style="color: gray;">&#128465;</span>
                            <p><strong>Non-food Zones</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="body-text">
                            Areas not exposed to food or splashes, but may be subject to some dirt or debris.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">6</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">ABB SAFETY SERIES FOOD & BEVERAGE</div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column">
                <div class="body-text">
                    <div class="icon-box">
                        <span style="color: blue;">&#127757;</span>
                        <p><strong>2 Environment</strong></p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        In a food and beverage production environment, <span class="highlight">lack of space can cause safety issues</span>. Limited space for wiring, air flow, and access to clean and sanitary equipment can create hazards. As advances in automation, hardware technology and control systems become more complex, the need for flexible designs that allow for reconfigurations within a certain area or existing facility footprint are invaluable. It's common for an F&B manufacturer to frequently modify equipment.
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        Another critical element is how a system is rated and performs in an environment with moisture, dust, or chemicals. Installation products are designed and tested to meet the rigorous requirements of the environment, including IP, which is a global certification and test, and the most desired rating by F&B processors is an IP69K protection rating.
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <span class="highlight">It is essential to know the installation facility plans</span> to ensure that the right products are selected for use with acidic, food alcohol, or additives.
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="column">
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <div class="icon-box">
                            <span style="color: green;">&#127757;</span>
                            <p><strong>Hygenic</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="body-text">
                            clean, sanitary, and contributes to health and disease prevention.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <div class="icon-box">
                            <span style="color: red;">&#128165;</span>
                            <p><strong>Antimicrobial</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="body-text">
                            kills or slows the spread of microorganisms.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <div class="icon-box">
                            <span style="color: purple;">&#128166;</span>
                            <p><strong>Bacteria-resistant</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="body-text">
                            inhibits growth of bacteria, fungus and mold.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">7</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">CONSIDERATIONS FOR BOOSTING PRODUCTIVITY AND PRESERVING SAFETY</div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column">
                <div class="body-text">
                    <div class="icon-box">
                        <span style="color: orange;">&#127757;</span>
                        <p><strong>3 Cleanability</strong></p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        Improving the degree of food safety in a facility can be achieved with proper material selection, correct ratings, and design features that make cleaning and sanitation easier.
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        A huge challenge food and beverage processors face is properly cleaning and sanitizing behind, between and underneath all equipment and components in processing areas. Depending on the type of processing, personnel can also pose a significant threat to cleanability.
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <div style="text-align: center; margin: 30px 0;">
                            <div style="font-size: 80px; font-weight: bold;">360°</div>
                            <p style="font-size: 14px;">In addition to the design and 360-degree cleanability of equipment, the selection of materials is critical to prevent bacteria and flaking and pose a safety threat.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="body-text">
                            For efficiency and thoroughness, F&B manufacturers should aim for smooth, rounded or sloped surfaces to prevent the accumulation of food and to meet proper ratings and certifications for the application and environment. Avoid the following:
                        </div>
                        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li class="list-item">Nicks, scratches, tool marks</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Sharp corners and crevices</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Cable bundling or looping</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Stickers and raised or recessed lettering</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Horizontal catches</li>
                        </ul>
                        <div class="body-text" style="margin-top: 20px;">
                            If you can clean it, you can use it is a familiar mantra in food processing. A single bacterial outbreak can wipe out decades of consumer trust and confidence.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="column">
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <div class="icon-box">
                            <span style="color: blue;">&#127757;</span>
                            <p><strong>Material selection considerations</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="body-text">
                            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                                <li class="list-item">Hygenic properties such as antimicrobial and bacteria-resistant materials and surfaces</li>
                                <li class="list-item">Offset ability to separate conduit, equipment and pipes from walls and allow for 360-degree cleaning</li>
                                <li class="list-item">Materials that are non-toxic and will not alter the taste, smell, appearance, or chemical composition of food or beverage if accidental contact is made.</li>
                                <li class="list-item">FDA-compliant material is also a big factor for food safety.</li>
                                <li class="list-item">Liquid ingress protection that keeps liquid out of the electrical system is one of the most important</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">8</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px;">ABB SAFETY SERIES FOOD & BEVERAGE</div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column">
                <div class="body-text">
                    <div class="icon-box">
                        <span style="color: red;">&#127757;</span>
                        <p><strong>4 Detectability</strong></p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        In food and beverage processing, detection is prevention. From raw ingredients to ready cut items, all F&B manufacturers must have at least one type of detection equipment such as metal or X-ray technology. Many producers use a combination of detection methods including:
                    </div>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li class="list-item">Metal detectors and magnets</li>
                        <li class="list-item">X-ray technology is increasingly used to identify glass, metal, porcelain, and bone fragments in meat and poultry.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="body-text" style="margin-top: 20px;">
                        Recognising that just because something is detectable, doesn't mean it's easily detected was a catalyst for innovation at ABB. To improve visual and metal detection, ABB introduced detectable Ty-Rap® cable ties in 2006. Continued innovation has resulted in Ty-Rap® cable ties that change color to warn of potentially dangerous high temperatures in equipment and components.
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        ABB also introduced antimicrobial ties for food processing, which are designed to prevent the growth of bacteria on the surface of the spacer.
                    </div>
                    <div class="body-text">
                        In food and beverage processing, detection is prevention.
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="column">
                    <div class="body-text">
                        <p>Fasteners are found at each stage of F&B processing and handling and throughout facilities, connecting everything from conveyor belts to system wiring. While some manufacturers use welded steel rings and loop systems, cable ties made of nylon and polypropylene materials are used to secure equipment and components. The cable market is estimated to grow by $1.4B billion during 2020-2024, fueled in part by demand for detectable ties.</p>
                        <p style="margin-top: 20px;">Recognising that just because something is detectable, doesn't mean it's easily detected was a catalyst for innovation at ABB. To improve visual and metal detection, ABB introduced detectable Ty-Rap® cable ties in 2006. Continued innovation has resulted in Ty-Rap® cable ties that change color to warn of potentially dangerous high temperatures in equipment and components. ABB also introduced antimicrobial ties for food processing, which are designed to prevent the growth of bacteria on the surface of the spacer.</p>
                        <p style="margin-top: 20px;">In food and beverage processing, detection is prevention.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>




<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 12pt; color: #555;">CONSIDERATIONS FOR BOOSTING PRODUCTIVITY AND PRESERVING SAFETY</div>
        <div style="font-size: 12pt; color: #555;">{{ page_number }}</div>
    </div>

    <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">The scope of sustainability is shifting and applies to the product and the process in the Food & Beverage sector.</h1>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 60px; margin-top: 40px;">
        <div style="flex: 1;">
            <div style="font-size: 36pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">5</div>
            <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 0;">Sustainability</h2>
            <p style="line-height: 1.6;">
                <span data-field="sustainability_summary">{{ sustainability_summary }}</span>
            </p>
            <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
                <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">Simplifying</div>
                <p style="line-height: 1.6;">and fostering use of recycled and reusable packaging.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 1.5; line-height: 1.6;">
            <p>As the scope of sustainability broadens beyond the source, quality and healthiness of ingredients, F&B manufacturers are demonstrating more than a desire for compliance in methods and materials. To align with national and international environmental protection guidelines and their own sustainability objectives, many are choosing recycled materials and products designed for reliability over a longer operating lifetime.</p>
            <p>The clear shift from focusing on upfront expense to consideration of equipment replacement costs and avoidance of waste is also leading more producers to move to long-term, sustainable solutions:</p>
            <ul style="padding-left: 20px;">
                <li><span data-field="sustainability_point_1">{{ sustainability_point_1 }}</span></li>
                <li><span data-field="sustainability_point_2">{{ sustainability_point_2 }}</span></li>
                <li><span data-field="sustainability_point_3">{{ sustainability_point_3 }}</span></li>
                <li><span data-field="sustainability_point_4">{{ sustainability_point_4 }}</span></li>
                <li><span data-field="sustainability_point_5">{{ sustainability_point_5 }}</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 12pt; color: #555;">10</div>
        <div style="font-size: 12pt; color: #555;">ABB SAFETY SERIES FOOD & BEVERAGE</div>
    </div>

    <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">Identifying a material or process at any point in the manufacturing cycle that can lead to a recall can be a huge wake-up call.</h1>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 60px; margin-top: 40px;">
        <div style="flex: 1;">
            <div style="font-size: 36pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">6</div>
            <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 0;">Harmonisation</h2>
            <p style="line-height: 1.6;">
                <span data-field="harmonisation_summary">{{ harmonisation_summary }}</span>
            </p>
            <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 20px;">Quick fixes and mating together disparate electrical components can pose significant threats in the washdown and processing areas. For example, if two IP69k components do not mate correctly, this will lead to liquid ingress. For this reason, IP69k flexible conduit systems will perform and hold up much better than an IP69k fitting alone. Because products from different manufacturers are not configured to work well together, it can make it more challenging to identify potential issues early, thereby increasing the likelihood of outages and downtime. F&B has a need to standardize on one manufacturer that can supply them with all their electrical system needs.</p>
            <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 20px;">Instead of trying to piece things together, F&B manufacturers should take into consideration the benefits of installing complete systems – including safety, energy efficiency, production continuity and support of digitisation efforts.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 1.5; line-height: 1.6;">
            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
                <div style="font-size: 24pt; margin-right: 15px;">&#9889;</div>
                <p style="font-weight: bold;">Innovation and higher standards of safety and sustainability are going into every aspect of food and beverage production, helping to avoid potential contamination risk in the industry.</p>
            </div>
            <p>With so much at stake, F&B producers can no longer take a trial and error approach and need to prioritise the selection of the correct products from a single right manufacturer. Ensuring that all electrical elements, from conduit and cable to fittings, are compatible and work in concert to enable the highest levels of safety and sustainability is a key benefit of ABB helping protect this critical industry at every phase.</p>
            <p>Not only do we look at the whole facility, but we leverage ABB expertise across the entire food and beverage processing spectrum. From farm to fork and every point in between, ABB products are needed in each F&B segment and application.</p>
            <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
                <div style="font-size: 24pt; margin-right: 15px;">&#9889;</div>
                <p style="font-weight: bold;">When F&B processors focus on harmonising electrical solutions and consistently maintaining, testing and training as a strategic part of their business, the result is improved compliance, food safety and uptime.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 12pt; color: #555;">11</div>
        <div style="font-size: 12pt; color: #555;">CONSIDERATIONS FOR BOOSTING PRODUCTIVITY AND PRESERVING SAFETY</div>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 60px; margin-top: 40px;">
        <div style="flex: 1;">
            <div style="font-size: 24pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">&#128100;</div>
            <p style="line-height: 1.6;">Instead of trying to piece things together, processors need to take into consideration the benefits of installing complete systems – including safety, energy efficiency, production continuity and support of digitisation efforts.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 1.5; line-height: 1.6;">
            <h3 style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px;">References</h3>
            <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
